---
title: 'Series Bars'
---

Bar-like series can have fixed widths in pixels or widths proportional to the category bands.

## Fixed Width

Use the `width` option on a bar-like series to set the pixel width of the bars.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Fixed Width" name="fixed-width" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'bar',
            width: 30,
        },
    ],
}
```

In this example:

-   The width of each bar in the series is set to 30 pixels.
-   Resizing the chart does not affect the width of the bars.
-   If the chart is too narrow, the bars will be clipped on the right-hand side.

## Clipping

When the widths of multiple bar-like series adds up to wider than the [series area](./layout/#chart-layout-calculation) of a chart, the bars will be clipped. The clipped bars can be viewed using the [Scrollbar](./scrollbar), [Navigator](./navigator) or [Zoom](./zoom) modules.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Fixed Width Clipping" name="fixed-width-clipping" type="generated" /%}

In this example:

-   Toggle the fixed width on and off. When off the bars are automatically sized to fit the width of the series area.
-   Use the slider to change the size of the width in pixels.
-   A [Scrollbar](./scrollbar) is used to allow the clipped bars to be viewed.

## Band Alignment

Use the `bandAlignment` option on a [Category](./axes-types/#category) or [Unit Time](./axes-time/#unit-time) axis to align fixed width bars.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Band Alignment" name="band-alignment" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    axes: {
        x: {
            type: 'category',
            bandAlignment: 'start',
        },
    },
}
```

In this example:

-   The category axis has an initial band alignment of start.
-   Use the buttons to compare other band alignment options.

## Width Ratio

Use the `widthRatio` option to set the bar width as a proportion of the default width.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Width Ratio" name="width-ratio" type="generated" /%}

When the series is ungrouped, with `grouped: false`, the width ratio will be relative to the full width of the category, including other series.

When the series is grouped, by default or with `grouped: true`, the width ratio will be relative to the automatically calculated width based on the size of the series area.

```js format="snippet"
{
    series: [
        {
            type: 'range-bar',
            grouped: false,
            widthRatio: 0.4,
        },
    ],
}
```

In this example:

-   The "Australia" series is ungrouped and has an initial width ratio of 0.4.
-   Use the slider to change the width ratio.
-   The bars will not be clipped, since they take up a proportion of the default width.

## Series Types

The `width` and `widthRatio` options can be used on [Bar](./bar-series), [Box Plot](./box-plot-series), [Range Bar](./range-bar-series) and [Waterfall](./waterfall-series) series.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Waterfall Width" name="waterfall-width" type="generated" /%}

## Actual vs Target Bars

{% chartExampleRunner title="Actual vs Target Bars" name="actual-target" type="generated" /%}

In this example:

-   The "Actual" series is ungrouped and has a width ratio of 0.7.
-   The "Satisfactory" and "Excellent" target series are grouped, and so each takes up half the category's width.
